Notes:
	ZERO-COST variant of AlexAligned_Unified_v7_Validate_TerminalWeights.rts -- identical in every
	way EXCEPT Commission and Slippage are both 0. Same Terminal_Weights.csv, same StartDate/
	EndDate, same Quantity/DynamicSizing logic, own separate output files (suffix _ZeroCost) so
	this run's results sit next to the cost-inclusive run's for direct comparison, not overwriting
	them.

	WHY THIS EXISTS: the first two real runs (with cost, then zero cost) swung wildly apart (+8.53%
	then +56.98%, vs the terminal's own +16.56%), which turned out to be a real semantic bug in the
	Quantity formula, now fixed (see the cost-inclusive script's Notes: for the full explanation --
	the CSV recomputes a fresh weight for a held symbol every date, but the terminal never re-weights
	an existing holding, so the old formula was constantly nibbling position sizes and RealTest was
	correctly logging each nibble as its own partial-exit trade). With that fixed (Shares <> 0 now
	skips resizing an existing holding), trade count should sit much closer to the terminal's own
	~960, at which point cost drag is a much smaller, more realistic factor. This zero-cost run still
	isolates it cleanly: with cost forced to zero, any remaining gap in return/drawdown against the
	terminal's own numbers is not a cost-model artifact -- it would point to something more
	structural (e.g. fill timing, or an actual disagreement in picks/weights) worth digging into.

	BEFORE RUNNING: same steps as the cost-inclusive script -- Terminal_Weights.csv must already be
	sitting next to this file in C:\RealTest21_newerv2\Scripts\SectorTerminalScripts, and the
	StartDate/EndDate below must match the window that CSV actually covers.

	Run Run_AlexAligned_v7_Validate_TerminalWeights_ZeroCost.bat (or the matching .ps1 directly).

Settings:
	DataFile:	C:\RealTest21_newerv2\Data\alexaligned_unified_v7.rtd
	BarSize:	Daily
	EndDate:	Latest
	AccountSize:	100000
	UseAvailableBars:	False
	SaveTradesAs:	?scriptpath?\AlexAligned_Unified_v7_Validate_TerminalWeights_ZeroCost_Trades.csv
	SaveTestListAs:	?scriptpath?\AlexAligned_Unified_v7_Validate_TerminalWeights_ZeroCost_Results.csv
	SaveStatsAs:	?scriptpath?\AlexAligned_Unified_v7_Validate_TerminalWeights_ZeroCost_Equity.csv

TestSettings:
	// CONFIRM these against the Terminal_Weights.csv you actually downloaded before running --
	// must match the cost-inclusive run's window exactly for a fair side-by-side comparison.
	StartDate:	2025-09-15
	EndDate:	2026-09-25

Data:
	DataValueFile:	?scriptpath?\Terminal_Weights.csv
	Weight:	#DataValueFile
	RebalCount:	#Count Weight

Strategy: TerminalWeights
	// No Side: line -- RealTest rejects "Side" on a DynamicSizing strategy; side is implied by the
	// sign of Quantity instead (always positive here, so long-only).
	MaxPositions:	60
	QtyType:	Percent
	DynamicSizing:	True
	// Shares <> 0 skips resizing an existing holding -- matches the terminal's own engine(),
	// which only weights brand-new buys, never re-weights a position already held. See the
	// cost-inclusive script's Notes: for the full explanation of why this fix was needed.
	Quantity:	Select(RebalCount = 0, nan, IsNaN(Weight), 0, Shares <> 0, nan, Weight * 100)
	Reduce:	0.01 * S.Alloc

	// The only difference from the cost-inclusive script: both forced to zero.
	Commission:	0
	Slippage:	0

Graphs:
	Equity:	Combined(S.Equity)
